  "configuration_id": "config_026",
  "reason": "Evidence: scvi_n200 outperforms pca_n2000 for RNA encoding (0.5203 vs 0.4849), and adding an image modality (resnet50 or ViT-L) improves over RNA-only by ~1.5-2%. However, all multimodal results so far use concat fusion; we have no evidence on whether weighted fusion is better or worse. Question: config_026 (scvi_n200 + resnet50 + weighted) is a single-variable change from our best config (config_004: concat, 0.5362), isolating the fusion strategy while holding RNA encoder, image encoder, and profile setting constant. Why this is the best next experiment: fusion is a fundamental design axis with zero coverage in the history, and resolving it early (weighted vs concat) will inform whether to invest remaining budget in multiprofile/aggregation variants. A single-variable comparison from the current best is the most efficient way to reduce uncertainty without confounding multiple factors."
}

